# ROADMAP-NS-DE1 — NORTHSTAR 1.1 CLI and agent tooling

File: openOODA/audit/roadmap_ns_de1.oot
Survey only. No product edit. No ROADMAP edit. Pin is v0.200.0-beta. C emit + gcc stays product.

Logline: This board compares NORTHSTAR 1.1 agent tooling and CLI-facing determinism and zero ambient to the live tree.
Setup: Read NORTHSTAR 1.1, SHIPPED, WORKFLOW §0, ooda/cli, ooda/lsp, vscode, the door, the guide, and registry.
Beats:
  1. Score JSON diagnostics, outline, reflect, fix, and patch.
  2. Score install and store ambient claims.
  3. Score CLI-facing determinism only.
  4. List recommended open rows. The list is empty.

## 1. Method

Production means a stranger or an agent cannot use the pin as NORTHSTAR 1.1 states.
That set is JSON diagnostics, outline and reflect, ooda fix and ooda patch, and no ambient grant in the published install and store story.
Do not open oodac leftovers. Do not open library leftovers. Do not open moonshots.
Paused install, HITL, and vscode `ooda-lsp.js` stay residual (ROADMAP 5.1).

## 2. Agent-native tooling (NORTHSTAR 1.1)

### 2.1 Structured JSON diagnostics
NORTHSTAR clause: Structured JSON diagnostics. The compiler prints machine diagnostics.
Disk proof: `ooda/oodac/diag_json.oo` arms `oodac check --json-errors` in process. `ooda/cli/json_check.oo` converts `ooda check --json-errors` from check text. SHIPPED: JSON errors carry line, col, and a nonempty path. Product CLI also converts. Locks: `ooda/scripts/json_errors_smoke.oo`, `ooda/scripts/test_json_errors.oo`.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: An agent can print a JSON array from `ooda check --json-errors` or `oodac check --json-errors` on the pin.

### 2.2 AST outline
NORTHSTAR clause: AST reflection. Agent query tools include `ooda outline`.
Disk proof: `ooda/cli/main.oo` forwards outline to `oodac`. `ooda/oodac/ast_emit_outline.oo` prints pub signatures and `--json` `{functions,verifies}`. SHIPPED names `outline`. Lock: `ooda/scripts/outline_reflect_smoke.oo`.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: An agent can list public names without the full source.

### 2.3 AST reflect
NORTHSTAR clause: AST reflection. Agent query tools include `ooda reflect`.
Disk proof: `ooda/oodac/ast_emit_reflect.oo` prints JSON kind, name, params, ret, requires, ensures, and caps. SHIPPED names `reflect`. Same lock as 2.2. Fixture `ooda/fixtures/outline_reflect_pass.oo` uses `FsCap`, not `FsReadCap`.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: Reflect runs. Caps in the fixture lock match `FsCap`. Params still carry product token types. Merkle cache (NORTHSTAR 3.3) is later, not 1.1.

### 2.4 Automated repair (`ooda fix`)
NORTHSTAR clause: Automated code repair (`ooda fix`).
Disk proof: `ooda/cli/fix_drive.oo` applies E_CAP, E_IMP, E_TC, E_PARSE, and E_MUST. Max eight passes. Asks unless `--yes`. Writes through `write_file` and `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`. SHIPPED names this set. Lock: `ooda/scripts/emust_autofix_smoke.oo`.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: An agent can repair the named classes with `--yes` and a write dir.

### 2.5 Surgical patch (`ooda patch`)
NORTHSTAR clause: Automated code repair (`ooda patch`).
Disk proof: `ooda/cli/patch_drive.oo` replaces one function body (`--replace-fn` / `--with`). Absolute paths, `..`, and symlinks refuse. SHIPPED names this. Guide `Options.oot` documents it.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: An agent can replace one function without a full rewrite.

## 3. Zero ambient (CLI, install, store)

### 3.1 Public install line
NORTHSTAR clause: Zero ambient authority. Published install must not grant implicit host rights.
Disk proof: Door `openOODA.github.io/index.html` prints `curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install | oo`. Payload `openOODA.github.io/install` is `.oo`. It prints wait text. WORKFLOW §0: payload is never `| sh`. Paused until the compiler and the library finish.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: The public line is not a shell. WORKFLOW and the guide say install waits. That fact stays residual (5.1).

### 3.2 `ooda install` floor
NORTHSTAR clause: Zero ambient authority on the install story.
Disk proof: `ooda/cli/cmd_more.oo` prints `ooda install: ok` and does not copy binaries. Later source `ooda/install/` is not the public first-machine path. SHIPPED does not claim a live public install.
Production requirement? no
Recommend open row? no
Why: The command is a floor stub. Opening a real installer would sell the paused path.

### 3.3 Store fetch and lock
NORTHSTAR clause: No implicit filesystem, net, or process grant in the store story.
Disk proof: `ooda/cli/cmd_pm_reg.oo` GETs `/catalog` and verifies minisign with `ooda/cli/registry.pub`. Extra caps and yank refuse. `ooda/cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo --exec` tests that the CAS path exists. It does not run a foreign ELF with extra tokens. SHIPPED: ingest allow-list and `add` are native. Guide `Packages.oot` matches. `registry/README.oot` still says the CLI does not fetch. That sentence is stale. The CLI does fetch.
Production requirement? yes
Recommend open row? no
Why: A stranger can add from the catalog with a pin and a declared cap. Extra rights refuse.

## 4. Determinism (CLI only)

### 4.1 File digest
NORTHSTAR clause: Zero-timestamp artifact digests.
Disk proof: `ooda/cli/cmd_digest.oo` prints sha256 of file bytes. SHIPPED names `digest`.
Production requirement? no
Recommend open row? no
Why: Digest is product. It does not claim a zero-timestamp compiler object.

### 4.2 Reproducible binaries
NORTHSTAR clause: Bit-identical compilation and reproducible binary outputs.
Disk proof: SHIPPED: two `emit-c` of hello are byte-identical. gcc binaries are not claimed without strip and repro flags. That leftover is ROADMAP 5.3.
Production requirement? no
Recommend open row? no
Why: CLI-facing determinism is emit identity. Raw gcc `cmp` is an oodac leftover. Do not add a row.

## 5. Adjacent facts (not new rows)

  CLI help in `ooda/cli/main.oo` still prints `0.199.0-alpha`. The pin is v0.200.0-beta. The tools still run.
  `ooda lsp` is a native stdio loop. Hover and definition use the ident under the cursor (`ooda/cli/lsp_reply.oo`). Lock: `ooda/scripts/lsp_cursor_smoke.oo`.
  Host `vscode/extension.js` starts `ooda lsp`. `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js` remains on disk. SHIPPED and ROADMAP 5.1 keep that residual. Do not open it.
  `ooda/cli/lsp/lsp_diagnostics.oo` exists. `lsp_drive.oo` does not publish those diagnostics. Agents use `check --json-errors` instead.
  Floor verbs `em`, `migrate`, `bench` print ok. They are not 1.1 agent tools.

## 6. Verdict

  JSON diagnostics, outline, reflect, fix, and patch exist on the pin.
  The public install line is paused and is not `| sh`.
  The store verifies the catalog and does not grant ambient caps.
  CLI determinism does not need a new row outside 5.3.
  C emit + gcc remains the product path.

## 7. Recommended open rows

  None.

